  "id": "COMPOUND:42136 - PROTEIN:5011",
  "verbalization": "Neoclovene is implicated in the biological activity of HCC1937 through a series of molecular interactions involving the MIP (Molecular Interaction Protein) pathway. The evidence suggests that Neoclovene acts as a target for multiple compounds, all of which are recognized as targets of HCC1937. This indicates a potential mechanism where Neoclovene may influence HCC1937 through the MIP, possibly by modulating its activity or binding to specific sites on the protein. The consistent involvement of MIP as a target in all three paths underscores a recurring mechanism, suggesting that Neoclovene may exert its effects via a shared pathway that ultimately leads to interactions with HCC1937. The presence of multiple distinct compounds all targeting HCC1937 further supports the idea that Neoclovene could be part of a broader network of molecules that interact with HCC1937 through the MIP, potentially influencing its function in a cellular context.",
